WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.293
Week 15: Health, Body, and Emergencies. describe symptoms understand basic medical questions request urgent help

2
00:00:08.293 --> 00:00:21.687
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can describe symptoms, understand basic medical questions, request urgent help. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:29.489
Language system. Doler and sentirse; body parts with definite articles; hace + time; emergency commands.

4
00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:35.947
Sound and delivery. Clear stress in medicine names, body terms, and emergency numbers.

5
00:00:35.947 --> 00:00:45.223
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:45.223 --> 00:01:09.156
Model language. Me duele mucho la cabeza. — My head hurts a lot. Tengo fiebre desde ayer. — I have had a fever since yesterday. ¿Es alérgico a algún medicamento? — Are you allergic to any medication? Llame a una ambulancia. — Call an ambulance. Se cayó y se lastimó el brazo. — He or she fell and hurt an arm.

7
00:01:09.156 --> 00:01:19.054
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
